+[[mcode:m54-m55]]
+== M54, M55 Resource Availability
+
+(((M54 Resource Acquire)))(((M55 Resource Release)))
+
+`M54` acquires one availability-controlled physical resource and
+`M55` releases it. A `P` word selects a joint number and the
+standard `$` word selects a spindle number:
+
+----
+M54 P2    (acquire joint 2)
+M55 P2    (release joint 2)
+M54 $0    (acquire spindle 0)
+M55 $0    (release spindle 0)
+----
+
+Exactly one selector is required. Joint numbers must be nonnegative integers;
+spindle group selectors such as `$-1` are not supported. These commands are
+ordered barriers: subsequent G-code is not executed until the transition has
+completed or failed. LinuxCNC does not pair resources or roll back a preceding
+transition automatically. M54 and M55 must be the only command in their block;
+comments and a line number are permitted. Motion, modal changes, other M-codes,
+parameter assignments, polar coordinates, and unsupported words are rejected
+before execution of block actions. Selectors must name one configured resource.
+
+The execution boundary is: finish preceding motion and IO, dispatch the runtime
+API request, wait for its shared completion boundary or failure, then continue.
+Required volatile-joint homing, planner reconciliation, and task/interpreter and
+canonical position synchronization are part of that runtime API completion for
+both NML/Python callers and M54. ACK alone does not permit continuation.
+Sequential M54/M55 blocks work in AUTO and MDI because each finishes before the
+next is interpreted. External direct requests require an idle task and cannot
+interrupt an in-program operation. Use Abort to cancel ACK wait or acquisition
+homing: it terminates the program and prevents subsequent blocks from executing,
+even if ACK arrives late. Ordinary M55/release does not cancel acquisition.
+Failure stops execution; subsequent blocks are not run. These M-codes use the same
+lifecycle as the NML/Python command API and provide no resource pairing or
+machine-specific switching sequence.
+
 [[mcode:m61]]
 == M61 Set Current Tool
 
